From 1b5374d2745d3458d8bce5d6b2059f7fad3a4eba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:50:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(kanban): annotation narrow key by origin
 content, not raw board/shadow revisions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The holder's narrow key (card B, e85501de30f) hashed every own board's and sync shadow's content
key verbatim. Those revisions move on any non-bookkeeping commit anywhere in the file, so on
hermes-hub the shared default board and its sync shadow moved every scope's key on nearly every
2 s probe: each of the 8 demanded scopes refreshed every 12 s (floor + probe) instead of every
20 s renewal, and the holder cost 17.9% of a core against a 2.4% budget (t_01a1db1387f61a98).

Five whys: the holder refreshed at the floor -> the narrow key moved every probe -> it carried
raw board/shadow revisions (plus 180 s buckets of ~11 owners' heartbeat clocks, plus the
chat-closeout waiting inputs, which embed every board's raw content key) -> C2 was measured on
linked shadow rows and referenced own-board content, but the key was built from the exact
fingerprint's inputs -> the benchmarks' synthetic stream never churned board/shadow revisions.

Now (new kanban_annotation_local):
- own boards: the open cards this profile's sessions own (session_id) or shepherd (tui notify
  sub) and their open ancestors: status, needs-human verdict, block_kind, human_request digest,
  watch flag. Claims, heartbeats, runs, events, comments and other origins' cards do not enter.
  Per-board reads are memoised on the board's content key, shared by every scope; a moved
  revision re-reads only the cards the per-task change cursor (kanban_task_change) names, or
  the whole board when the cursor cannot vouch for the gap. Session-id lookups read only ids
  not yet checked.
- sync shadows: this origin's unreleased link rows joined to their cards (the replica_cards
  rows, same memo via kanban_chat_links.replica_link_rows), minus lease_expires, plus the
  replica's stale verdict.
- gateway info observed_at clocks and last_ok enter as freshness verdicts at now, not buckets.
- waiting sources enter by code identity, not their declared inputs.
- past the floor the holder probe answers from the narrow key alone; the exact fingerprint
  (waiting-input probes) is read only when no narrow verdict exists.
Strict callers keep the exact fingerprint unchanged; any read error is None (= moved).
Display state the key omits (unseen cursors, run liveness, stall verdicts) stays bounded by the
20 s forced renewal, as before.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_annotation_narrow_local.py — 10 of the liveness/other-origin
cases fail on the old key; status, membership and link changes move both; patched board rows
equal a full read under random churn.

Benchmark (scripts/benchmark_kanban_annotation_holder.py) now churns a real own board and sync
shadow every window: raw revisions moved in 150/150 windows, the key in 0 of 84-98 windows
without an own substantive change (large tier, 10k cards, also with a 400 MB WAL: 37 ms/key).
Live hub replay (8 scopes, 120 x 5 s, same files): old key moved 110-115 times per scope, new
key 0 times in all 7 non-default scopes.
